                <pb facs="0255" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/444.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Cruisers <hi rendition="#italic">North Carolina</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi> left on the 8th instant at midnight. I am informed by the
                    minister for foreign affairs that Morales has made a landing and is in hiding in
                    the neighborhood of Pedro Macoris and that yesterday an expedition under
                    Desiderio Arias left Nipe, Cuba, presumably for Monte Christi. The gunboat <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wheeling</hi> is here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
